schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: KOI-net reached public beta in May 2025 and is actively maintained
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    KOI-net, the network protocol and Python framework implementing RID-based
    federation, hit public beta in May 2025, is MIT-licensed, and is actively
    maintained (v2.0.7 as of May 2026, per `koi-net` on GitHub).
  evidence: 'Cited to the BlockScience/koi-net GitHub repository.'
  source_lineage: 'https://github.com/BlockScience/koi-net'
  interpretation: >-
    Supports the article's framing of KOI-net as a credible, currently-usable
    protocol option (not vaporware) for teams ready to move beyond ad hoc
    "federate by hand" sharing.
  uncertainty: >-
    Version/maintenance status was not independently re-checked against the
    live repository at ingestion time; verify current version before citing
    externally.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/federation-portability.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
